# frozen_string_literal: true

# RegisteredTools — APP-OWNED, yours to edit.
#
# This is the ONE place that lists what the AI may call: the allow-list. McpController
# passes `RegisteredTools.all` to `MCP::Server` on every request, and the `mcp` gem
# lists and calls only the classes in that array — there is no generic executor and no
# console tool.
#
# To expose a tool, add its class to the array below. To stop exposing one, remove it.
# That is the whole registration model: an ordinary Ruby array of tool classes.
#
# `.all` is called per request so the classes are named fresh each time — safe across
# a Zeitwerk dev reload (no cached, stale class objects).
module RegisteredTools
  def self.all
    [
      ExampleReadOnlyTool
    ]
  end
end
